<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The label colour for one half of a two-option preference toggle on the profile screen.

    A colour state list rather than two colours set in code: the fragment marks one half selected and
    both the fill (bg_profile_segment.xml) and this file answer that single state, so nothing about
    how the control looks lives in Kotlin. The filter chips on the Tasks tab are built the same way —
    see res/color/filter_chip_text.xml.

    **The chosen half takes `colorOnSelectedContainer`**, which is the accent in light mode and the
    near-black in dark. That pairing is not arbitrary: the fill it sits on is
    `colorSelectedContainer`, which is near-black in light mode and the accent in dark, and these two
    roles are defined as a matched pair precisely so that text placed on one is guaranteed legible
    (see attrs.xml). Naming a literal colour here instead would produce yellow-on-yellow in dark mode.

    The unchosen half takes the muted text colour on the track showing through behind it, so the two
    halves differ in weight as well as in fill — which is what makes the chosen one findable without
    reading either word.
-->
<selector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <item
        android:color="?attr/colorOnSelectedContainer"
        android:state_selected="true" />

    <item android:color="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

</selector>
